{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Now I understand the schemas:\n\nFarmers markets data:\n- state_name, state_abbr, farmers_markets (the count), and other columns\n\nCensus data:\n- NAME (state name), POPESTIMATE2025 (or possibly another year depending on what's requested), and other columns with sumlev=40 for states\n\nThe question asks for \"how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents\" - so I need to:\n1. Sum up all farmers markets from the farmers markets table\n2. Get the total U.S. population from the census table\n3. Calculate: (total farmers markets / total population) * 100,000\n\nLet me look at a few rows to understand the census data better.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_014UtjVRtnb6TJJBkLzXEm2j","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census","compose":"source.limit(5)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":276,"cacheRead":15555,"cacheWrite":1465,"totalTokens":17310,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0013800000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0015555000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00183125,"total":0.00478075},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":173},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915312698,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78RckyRRfuvhr3hrbRA","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_014UtjVRtnb6TJJBkLzXEm2j","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"SUMLEV\",\"REGION\",\"DIVISION\",\"STATE\",\"NAME\",\"ESTIMATESBASE2020\",\"POPESTIMATE2020\",\"POPESTIMATE2021\",\"POPESTIMATE2022\",\"POPESTIMATE2023\",\"POPESTIMATE2024\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\",\"NPOPCHG_2020\",\"NPOPCHG_2021\",\"NPOPCHG_2022\",\"NPOPCHG_2023\",\"NPOPCHG_2024\",\"NPOPCHG_2025\",\"BIRTHS2020\",\"BIRTHS2021\",\"BIRTHS2022\",\"BIRTHS2023\",\"BIRTHS2024\",\"BIRTHS2025\",\"DEATHS2020\",\"DEATHS2021\",\"DEATHS2022\",\"DEATHS2023\",\"DEATHS2024\",\"D